course: dictionary
lesson: 11877
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word braces is one of them. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «Mia has to wear braces to make her teeth straight» is about teeth, because straight and teeth are clues.
explain: Now read «Put the numbers inside braces: { 1, 2, 3 }». The clues are numbers and the curly shapes, so braces here means the curly brackets used in writing and maths.
explain: Grandad says, «My braces hold my trousers up.» In Britain, braces are straps that go over the shoulders. Americans call them suspenders. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Braces can mean wires on teeth, straps for trousers, supports for a weak joint, or curly brackets { } in writing and maths.
fact: «Braces» on teeth are used to make them straight over time.
fact: «Brace» supports something firmly in place, such as «Ben's knee brace».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Mia has to wear braces to make her teeth straight.» What are braces in this sentence? | *Wires fixed to the teeth to make them straight | Straps that go over the shoulders | Curly brackets used in maths
exercise: «Put the numbers inside braces: { 1, 2, 3 }.» Where do you see braces like this? | *In maths and writing | In the sea | At the dentist only | On a bike
exercise: Grandad says his braces hold his trousers up. In Britain, what do braces mean here? | *Straps that go over the shoulders | Curly brackets { } | A pair of shoes | Wires on teeth
test: «Ben wears a knee brace when he plays football.» What does a knee brace do? | Warms the knee in winter | *Holds an injured knee firmly in place | Makes the knee bend more | Keeps the football dry
test: Mia wears braces, so she must avoid which food? | Soft bread | *Sticky or hard sweets | Water | Cheese
exam: Which meaning fits «Ben's knee brace stopped his leg from wobbling»? | *Supports that hold something firmly in place | Wires fixed to teeth | Curly brackets { } | Straps that go over the shoulders
